1
00:00:09,480 --> 00:00:10,421
You ought to go!

2
00:00:21,940 --> 00:00:23,058
Keep an eye on him!

3
00:00:25,360 --> 00:00:26,260
No, wait!

4
00:00:36,480 --> 00:00:37,310
Damn!

5
00:00:42,180 --> 00:00:44,533
Where the hell does he think he's going?

6
00:00:51,600 --> 00:00:52,430
Shit.

7
00:01:06,300 --> 00:01:08,359
I don't know if I can't believe it.

8
00:01:10,300 --> 00:01:17,137
I don't know if I

9
00:01:17,220 --> 00:01:22,857
can't believe it.

10
00:01:52,492 --> 00:01:55,937
Meburu chisana oh my.

11
00:01:58,480 --> 00:02:02,417
Kizuku yawai watashi Game ga yleba.

12
00:02:07,640 --> 00:02:13,080
Nagai yume miru koro wa so aehen des.

13
00:02:14,640 --> 00:02:17,257
I wanna always be with you!

14
00:02:17,340 --> 00:02:20,180
I'm giving you everything I have.

15
00:02:33,140 --> 00:02:34,320
You idiot!

16
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:35,796
What's your problem?

17
00:02:38,540 --> 00:02:40,360
Well, what happened?

18
00:02:41,580 --> 00:02:42,940
I lost him.

19
00:02:43,120 --> 00:02:44,767
He Teleport off somewhere.

20
00:02:45,360 --> 00:02:48,820
The system's supposed to
protect players inside the inns.

21
00:02:49,060 --> 00:02:51,740
I thought if anywhere,
she'd be safe in here.

22
00:02:52,960 --> 00:02:53,790
Damn it!

23
00:02:55,380 --> 00:02:57,460
That robe was Griselda's.

24
00:02:59,100 --> 00:03:01,040
That was Griselda's ghost.

25
00:03:02,200 --> 00:03:04,500
She's come back to get revenge on us.

26
00:03:05,780 --> 00:03:07,020
Think about it.

27
00:03:07,340 --> 00:03:09,869
Only a ghost can PK
someone in a safe zone.

28
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:13,400
That wasn't a ghost.

29
00:03:15,140 --> 00:03:17,197
Someone's using the system to kill.

30
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:20,537
That's the only way these murders
could have happened in a safe zone.

31
00:03:20,620 --> 00:03:21,660
I know it.

32
00:03:26,580 --> 00:03:28,180
I don't know what to think.

33
00:03:28,460 --> 00:03:31,107
Was that black-robed
figure Griselda's ghost?

34
00:03:32,020 --> 00:03:36,800
After seeing two people die mysteriously,
I'm starting to think it's possible.

35
00:03:37,460 --> 00:03:38,290
No.

36
00:03:38,373 --> 00:03:40,220
That definitely wasn't a ghost.

37
00:03:41,260 --> 00:03:42,737
I'd bet my life on it.

38
00:03:42,820 --> 00:03:45,291
Why would a ghost need a teleport crystal?

39
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:48,200
Teleport crystal. What is it?

40
00:03:50,040 --> 00:03:51,680
Nah, it's nothing.

41
00:04:01,800 --> 00:04:02,630
Here.

42
00:04:03,900 --> 00:04:05,240
What is that for me?

43
00:04:05,760 --> 00:04:07,477
Well, what do you think I'm doing?

44
00:04:07,560 --> 00:04:08,390
Showing it off?

45
00:04:08,473 --> 00:04:10,401
Are you going to take it or what?

46
00:04:10,580 --> 00:04:12,220
Okay, thanks. Thank you.

47
00:04:14,020 --> 00:04:16,357
Better eat it fast before it disappears.

48
00:04:16,440 --> 00:04:18,675
Its durability is almost down to zero.

49
00:04:19,240 --> 00:04:20,360
Oh, uh, right.

50
00:04:25,960 --> 00:04:26,842
It's delicious.

51
00:04:29,620 --> 00:04:31,977
When the heck do you find
time to pick this up?

52
00:04:32,060 --> 00:04:34,897
I had a feeling we wouldn't
have time for lunch today.

53
00:04:34,980 --> 00:04:36,917
So this morning I packed one for us.

54
00:04:37,000 --> 00:04:38,529
Hurry up and eat it, okay?

55
00:04:39,260 --> 00:04:40,495
Gotta hand it to you.

56
00:04:40,640 --> 00:04:43,517
For a second in command of the
Knights of the Blood Oath, You rock.

57
00:04:43,600 --> 00:04:45,277
Where'd you buy these, anyway?

58
00:04:45,360 --> 00:04:47,200
I didn't. Huh?

59
00:04:48,180 --> 00:04:49,140
I made it.

60
00:04:49,820 --> 00:04:51,860
Yes, I can cook, so what?

61
00:04:55,240 --> 00:04:56,237
Wow, I...

62
00:04:56,320 --> 00:04:57,997
I don't even know what to say.

63
00:04:58,080 --> 00:05:02,904
I mean, if you're looking for a second
career, you'd make a killing selling these.

64
00:05:08,280 --> 00:05:10,927
Oh, should've been eating
instead of talking.

65
00:05:15,520 --> 00:05:16,800
Are you crying?

66
00:05:19,320 --> 00:05:20,380
No way!

67
00:05:21,100 --> 00:05:22,000
That's right.

68
00:05:22,300 --> 00:05:23,160
That's it!

69
00:05:23,980 --> 00:05:24,900
What's it?

70
00:05:25,140 --> 00:05:26,846
What did you just figure out?

71
00:05:27,460 --> 00:05:28,290
I...

72
00:05:28,373 --> 00:05:29,203
No, wait.

73
00:05:29,720 --> 00:05:31,420
We never saw a thing.

74
00:05:31,740 --> 00:05:35,152
We just thought we did, but
we were seeing something else.

75
00:05:35,620 --> 00:05:36,820
I was right.

76
00:05:37,400 --> 00:05:40,440
The game doesn't allow
killing inside a safe zone.

77
00:05:40,660 --> 00:05:42,778
There's no weapon or system exploit.

78
00:05:47,860 --> 00:05:48,690
Griselda

79
00:05:49,820 --> 00:05:51,857
The only way I can be saved now.

80
00:05:51,940 --> 00:05:53,175
Is if you forgive me.

81
00:05:54,880 --> 00:05:55,757
I'm sorry.

82
00:05:55,840 --> 00:05:57,077
I'm so sorry.

83
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:58,897
Please forgive me, Griselda.

84
00:05:58,980 --> 00:06:00,337
I swear.

85
00:06:00,420 --> 00:06:02,457
I never thought this was going to happen.

86
00:06:02,540 --> 00:06:03,893
You have to believe me.

87
00:06:07,520 --> 00:06:08,660
Oh really!

88
00:06:35,000 --> 00:06:36,740
What did you do to me?

89
00:06:37,020 --> 00:06:38,260
Tell me, Schmidt.

90
00:06:39,160 --> 00:06:40,760
Tell me what you did.

91
00:06:41,000 --> 00:06:42,100
Tell me now.

92
00:06:44,380 --> 00:06:45,497
Okay, okay.

93
00:06:45,580 --> 00:06:47,057
The day we voted to sell the ring,

94
00:06:47,140 --> 00:06:51,787
I looked at my belt pouch and there was
a crystal and a note with instructions.

95
00:06:51,920 --> 00:06:53,240
Who were they from?

96
00:06:54,660 --> 00:06:56,500
Who gave you them?

97
00:07:00,880 --> 00:07:02,660
Grimlock, you're dead too?

98
00:07:04,020 --> 00:07:04,940
Tell me.

99
00:07:05,240 --> 00:07:08,005
I want to know who gave
you those instructions.

100
00:07:08,340 --> 00:07:09,170
I don't know!

101
00:07:09,320 --> 00:07:10,555
I swear I don't know!

102
00:07:10,980 --> 00:07:14,377
The note said for me to bind
the crystal to Grisolda's room

103
00:07:14,460 --> 00:07:17,557
at the inn she was staying at
so whoever it was could get in.

104
00:07:17,640 --> 00:07:20,837
Then I had to put the crystal
in the guild's shared storage.

105
00:07:20,920 --> 00:07:21,750
Then what?

106
00:07:22,700 --> 00:07:24,240
That's all I did! I swear!

107
00:07:25,360 --> 00:07:26,831
I didn't want her to die!

108
00:07:27,000 --> 00:07:28,941
I didn't want to be part of that!

109
00:07:29,100 --> 00:07:29,930
Please!

110
00:07:30,013 --> 00:07:30,843
Believe me!

111
00:07:37,960 --> 00:07:40,560
We recorded everything you said, Schmidt.

112
00:07:50,660 --> 00:07:52,180
Wait, they're alive?

113
00:07:52,860 --> 00:07:54,400
Yup, they're alive.

114
00:07:54,840 --> 00:07:56,940
Both Caynz and Yorko.

115
00:07:58,680 --> 00:08:02,209
Inside safe zones, a player's
HP doesn't deplete on its own.

116
00:08:02,300 --> 00:08:04,476
But the durability of an object does.

117
00:08:04,740 --> 00:08:06,717
Just like that sandwich you gave me.

118
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:07,820
What?

119
00:08:08,320 --> 00:08:11,720
That day, the spear was
sticking out of Kynes' armor.

120
00:08:12,020 --> 00:08:14,020
It wasn't draining his HP, though.

121
00:08:14,260 --> 00:08:16,848
It was draining the
durability of his armor.

122
00:08:17,320 --> 00:08:22,820
But then, his body didn't disintegrate.
It was… Yup. Just his armor. Nothing else.

123
00:08:23,160 --> 00:08:27,240
And at the precise second when his
armor's durability expired, poof.

124
00:08:27,680 --> 00:08:30,621
Caynz used a crystal to
teleport out of his armor.

125
00:08:31,760 --> 00:08:35,878
Sure, it looks a lot like what happens
when a player dies in the game.

126
00:08:36,160 --> 00:08:37,540
Only he didn't die.

127
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,386
Then what happened to Yorkel?

128
00:08:41,600 --> 00:08:44,357
I bet the dagger was rigged
to her back the whole time.

129
00:08:44,440 --> 00:08:46,120
She had it all planned out.

130
00:08:46,340 --> 00:08:47,557
But we would have seen.

131
00:08:47,640 --> 00:08:49,537
Only if she turned around, though.

132
00:08:49,620 --> 00:08:52,091
Remember, she never turned her back to us.

133
00:08:52,220 --> 00:08:53,300
Not even once.

134
00:08:53,900 --> 00:08:57,697
She kept an eye on her equipment's
durability level while she was talking.

135
00:08:57,780 --> 00:08:59,251
When it got down to zero,

136
00:08:59,480 --> 00:09:02,417
all she had to do was act
like she was hit by a dagger,

137
00:09:02,500 --> 00:09:04,324
thrown from outside the window.

138
00:09:05,200 --> 00:09:07,857
Who was the person in the
black robe you chased?

139
00:09:07,940 --> 00:09:10,457
It wasn't Grimlock, I'm
pretty sure of that.

140
00:09:10,540 --> 00:09:11,520
But Caynz?

141
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:13,940
He and Yoriko were in it together.

142
00:09:14,280 --> 00:09:18,157
They figured out how they could use
this method to fake their own deaths.

143
00:09:18,240 --> 00:09:22,537
Getting people to think they were murdered
in a safe zone was a calculated twist.

144
00:09:22,620 --> 00:09:24,777
Everything they did was
designed to draw out the

145
00:09:24,860 --> 00:09:28,220
person behind Griselda's
murder and expose him.

146
00:09:28,560 --> 00:09:30,917
The only way to find out
for sure was by faking

147
00:09:31,000 --> 00:09:33,337
their deaths and creating
an illusionary Avenger.

148
00:09:33,420 --> 00:09:38,126
And Schmidt was the person they had picked
for it, probably since the beginning.

149
00:09:38,360 --> 00:09:41,820
Hey, you still have Yorko on
your friend list, don't you?

150
00:09:45,900 --> 00:09:48,312
Right now she's in the field on floor 19.

151
00:09:48,540 --> 00:09:52,940
It looks like she's on a small
hill, just outside of town. I see.

152
00:09:54,700 --> 00:09:55,582
That's it then.

153
00:09:55,820 --> 00:09:57,737
I guess they can handle it from here.

154
00:09:57,820 --> 00:10:01,173
I mean, our job's pretty much
done now, wouldn't you say?

155
00:10:02,180 --> 00:10:03,010
Mm-hmm.

156
00:10:08,340 --> 00:10:10,260
You were recording?

157
00:10:14,800 --> 00:10:16,500
So, that's how it is, huh?

158
00:10:17,480 --> 00:10:20,539
You cared about what happened
to Griselda after all.

159
00:10:20,780 --> 00:10:24,917
Of course we did, but you didn't betray
her because you hated her, did you?

160
00:10:25,000 --> 00:10:27,120
No, I didn't hate her, honest.

161
00:10:27,640 --> 00:10:28,470
I mean,

162
00:10:28,600 --> 00:10:31,337
sure, I feel guilty getting
money for my part of it,

163
00:10:31,420 --> 00:10:34,837
but the rare weapon I bought helped
me get into the Holy Dragon Alliance,

164
00:10:34,920 --> 00:10:35,750
so...

165
00:10:45,960 --> 00:10:46,790
Paralysis?

166
00:10:49,660 --> 00:10:50,620
One down!

167
00:10:55,260 --> 00:10:56,220
No way!

168
00:10:58,740 --> 00:11:00,620
That's a hell of a catch.

169
00:11:01,100 --> 00:11:04,380
A big shot from the Holy Dragon Alliance.

170
00:11:11,540 --> 00:11:14,420
Laughing Coffin, the Murder Guild.

171
00:11:20,740 --> 00:11:23,960
Alright, what game should
we play with these three?

172
00:11:24,260 --> 00:11:25,777
Oh, I know! I know!

173
00:11:25,860 --> 00:11:28,017
Let's play the one where
they have to kill each other

174
00:11:28,100 --> 00:11:31,300
last one standing wins I
know it's your favorite,

175
00:11:31,460 --> 00:11:33,877
but last time we did that
you killed the winner anyway.

176
00:11:33,960 --> 00:11:36,020
Oh, come on You spoiled it.

177
00:11:36,160 --> 00:11:38,631
It's no fun if they know they're gonna die

178
00:11:42,240 --> 00:11:45,640
All right, let's get this show on the road

179
00:11:56,420 --> 00:11:57,250
Huh?

180
00:12:09,120 --> 00:12:09,950
Damn.

181
00:12:11,360 --> 00:12:13,400
Looks like I made it just in time.

182
00:12:18,100 --> 00:12:19,640
So, now what?

183
00:12:19,940 --> 00:12:22,646
I got 30 players from
the assault team coming.

184
00:12:22,960 --> 00:12:25,136
You guys want to stay and fight them?

185
00:12:42,560 --> 00:12:43,840
Come on.

186
00:13:00,160 --> 00:13:02,300
Nice to see you alive again, Yorko.

187
00:13:03,280 --> 00:13:07,877
You won't believe me, but after it was
over, I was going to tell you the truth.

188
00:13:07,960 --> 00:13:10,720
I am sorry we had to
trick you to help us out.

189
00:13:13,060 --> 00:13:16,960
Kirito, thank you for saving me,
but how did you figure it out?

190
00:13:17,300 --> 00:13:19,657
How did you know those
three would attack us here?

191
00:13:19,740 --> 00:13:21,460
I didn't figure anything out.

192
00:13:21,700 --> 00:13:23,524
I was acting on a hunch is all.

193
00:13:24,080 --> 00:13:27,200
Hey, Yorko, Caynz, level with me.

194
00:13:27,460 --> 00:13:31,460
You guys asked Grimlock to make the
spear and the knife, didn't you?

195
00:13:32,580 --> 00:13:35,815
We did, but he was against
our plan from the beginning.

196
00:13:36,220 --> 00:13:39,460
All he wanted was to let
Griselda rest in peace.

197
00:13:39,660 --> 00:13:41,620
He did forge the weapons for us,

198
00:13:41,720 --> 00:13:44,817
but only after we got down
on our knees and begged him.

199
00:13:44,900 --> 00:13:48,177
Sorry, but he had a different
reason for not liking your plan.

200
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:50,319
Griselda had nothing to do with it.

201
00:13:50,840 --> 00:13:55,177
He was worried faking PKs in a safe zone
was going to draw a lot of attention.

202
00:13:55,260 --> 00:13:59,277
He didn't want to take the risk of
someone snooping around for answers.

203
00:13:59,360 --> 00:14:02,536
We figured the whole thing
out about half an hour ago.

204
00:14:05,980 --> 00:14:09,333
We ended up playing right into
Yoriko's hands, didn't we?

205
00:14:09,620 --> 00:14:10,450
You know what?

206
00:14:10,533 --> 00:14:12,720
I don't really mind. Yeah, me neither.

207
00:14:16,260 --> 00:14:18,137
Hey, if you were in their guild,

208
00:14:18,220 --> 00:14:22,102
and a super rare item like that
dropped, what would you have done?

209
00:14:22,980 --> 00:14:23,810
Oh, I don't know.

210
00:14:23,893 --> 00:14:24,920
I play solo.

211
00:14:25,220 --> 00:14:28,514
Part of why I do is so I can
avoid situations like that.

212
00:14:30,120 --> 00:14:32,237
In my guild, the one who
got the kill gets it.

213
00:14:32,320 --> 00:14:34,577
Those are the rules we have to play by.

214
00:14:34,660 --> 00:14:37,077
You know how in SAO, if
a player gets a drop,

215
00:14:37,160 --> 00:14:39,677
no one knows unless
that person reports it?

216
00:14:39,760 --> 00:14:44,497
Our way, no one can hoard stuff because
we worked out who gets what ahead of time.

217
00:14:44,580 --> 00:14:45,410
Also,

218
00:14:45,493 --> 00:14:49,801
the rules my guilt play by gives the concept
of marriage in this world real meaning.

219
00:14:50,020 --> 00:14:50,902
Think about it.

220
00:14:51,080 --> 00:14:53,977
If you marry, you have to
share your item storage.

221
00:14:54,060 --> 00:14:55,060
If you're single,

222
00:14:55,180 --> 00:14:57,297
you can hide whatever
you want, but, you know,

223
00:14:57,380 --> 00:15:00,145
when you're married, you
can't hide it anymore.

224
00:15:00,600 --> 00:15:04,777
I think sharing storage with the person
you're married to is wonderfully pragmatic.

225
00:15:04,860 --> 00:15:07,840
At the same time, I think
it's also very romantic.

226
00:15:10,920 --> 00:15:12,380
Hey. Yeah? What?

227
00:15:14,180 --> 00:15:17,298
So, uh, how many times have
you been married, anyway?

228
00:15:20,000 --> 00:15:21,217
Wait, I didn't mean it!

229
00:15:21,300 --> 00:15:22,437
That didn't come out right!

230
00:15:22,520 --> 00:15:25,257
You were talking about how it's
romantic and plastic and...

231
00:15:25,340 --> 00:15:27,180
I did not say that, you ass!

232
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:30,269
What I said is it's
romantic and pragmatic.

233
00:15:30,820 --> 00:15:34,720
For your information, the word
pragmatic means practical. My god.

234
00:15:35,060 --> 00:15:38,700
You think marriage in SAO
is practical? Of course.

235
00:15:39,040 --> 00:15:40,977
If you're married,
everything's out in the open,

236
00:15:41,060 --> 00:15:43,178
you know, because of common storage.

237
00:15:44,180 --> 00:15:45,010
What?

238
00:15:46,400 --> 00:15:47,230
That's it.

239
00:15:47,313 --> 00:15:48,340
Common storage.

240
00:15:48,820 --> 00:15:50,600
Okay, say your spouse dies.

241
00:15:50,920 --> 00:15:52,449
What happens to the items?

242
00:15:53,540 --> 00:15:55,460
Item storage is shared, right?

243
00:15:55,840 --> 00:15:59,020
So when one person dies,
what happens to their stuff?

244
00:16:00,120 --> 00:16:05,237
If you're talking about Griselda and
Grimlock, hmm, if one of them died...

245
00:16:05,320 --> 00:16:08,320
Everything would go to the
surviving spouse, right?

246
00:16:09,160 --> 00:16:12,957
And if everything goes to the spouse,
then the ring in Griselda's storage...

247
00:16:13,040 --> 00:16:16,157
...should be sitting in Grimlock's
storage, not the killer's.

248
00:16:16,240 --> 00:16:18,157
It's been sitting there this whole time.

249
00:16:18,240 --> 00:16:20,534
It was never stolen in the first place.

250
00:16:21,180 --> 00:16:22,580
No, it was stolen.

251
00:16:22,820 --> 00:16:24,697
It doesn't matter it's still there.

252
00:16:24,780 --> 00:16:29,133
Grimlock was basically stealing it the
minute he put his plan into action.

253
00:16:33,000 --> 00:16:34,220
It was Grimlock?

254
00:16:35,380 --> 00:16:37,321
Then those were his instructions.

255
00:16:37,940 --> 00:16:39,587
And he killed Griselda, too.

256
00:16:39,940 --> 00:16:42,940
No, I doubt he was the one
who actually killed her.

257
00:16:43,240 --> 00:16:48,064
Although, I'm pretty sure he went and found
himself a red player to do it for him.

258
00:16:48,940 --> 00:16:49,770
My God.

259
00:16:50,420 --> 00:16:52,637
But then if he really did have her killed,

260
00:16:52,720 --> 00:16:55,797
why would he go to all that
trouble just to help us out?

261
00:16:55,880 --> 00:16:59,760
You explained your plan to
him in detail, didn't you?

262
00:17:00,960 --> 00:17:03,277
Your plan was the perfect
chance for him to bury

263
00:17:03,360 --> 00:17:06,478
the ring incident and any
witnesses once and for all.

264
00:17:06,920 --> 00:17:09,840
All he'd have to do is
sit back and wait for you,

265
00:17:10,080 --> 00:17:12,037
Schmidt, and Caynz to get together.

266
00:17:12,120 --> 00:17:13,640
You'd be sitting ducks.

267
00:17:15,380 --> 00:17:16,210
That's it.

268
00:17:16,340 --> 00:17:17,180
That's why.

269
00:17:17,620 --> 00:17:20,267
They knew we'd be here
because he hired them.

270
00:17:20,560 --> 00:17:21,390
Yeah.

271
00:17:21,520 --> 00:17:25,579
My guess is it was probably the same
bunch he hired to kill Griselda.

272
00:17:26,760 --> 00:17:27,860
Oh my god.

273
00:17:30,660 --> 00:17:31,490
Found him.

274
00:17:36,480 --> 00:17:39,715
If you want to know more,
you can ask the man yourself.

275
00:17:44,120 --> 00:17:44,950
Hello.

276
00:17:45,033 --> 00:17:46,320
Long time no see, comrades.

277
00:17:47,080 --> 00:17:48,540
I can't believe it.

278
00:17:49,540 --> 00:17:50,477
Did you...

279
00:17:50,560 --> 00:17:52,440
did you really plan this?

280
00:17:54,240 --> 00:17:56,640
How could you, Grimlock? Answer me!

281
00:17:56,820 --> 00:17:58,349
Why did you kill Griselda?

282
00:17:58,520 --> 00:17:59,520
Was it the money?

283
00:17:59,620 --> 00:18:03,796
Was the money so important to you
that you'd kill your own wife for it?

284
00:18:05,140 --> 00:18:05,970
Money?

285
00:18:06,580 --> 00:18:07,980
Did you say money?

286
00:18:13,880 --> 00:18:15,360
It wasn't for the money.

287
00:18:15,860 --> 00:18:16,820
I had to.

288
00:18:17,060 --> 00:18:20,417
No matter what, I had to kill her
while we were stuck in this world.

289
00:18:20,500 --> 00:18:23,320
I had to kill her while
she was still my wife.

290
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:27,500
And because she was also
my wife in the real world.

291
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:32,400
In a way, she was the perfect wife. Ideal.

292
00:18:32,620 --> 00:18:34,580
So pretty, so submissive.

293
00:18:35,120 --> 00:18:38,417
The whole time we were together,
we never had a single fight.

294
00:18:38,500 --> 00:18:43,820
But when we were trapped in
here, in this world, she changed.

295
00:18:45,520 --> 00:18:50,040
In here, I was the one who was afraid,
terrified of playing this death game.

296
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:56,360
But she looked so much happier here, more
alive than she ever did in the real world.

297
00:18:57,760 --> 00:18:59,995
There was nothing I could do about it.

298
00:19:00,160 --> 00:19:01,200
She changed.

299
00:19:01,480 --> 00:19:03,140
The Yuuki I loved was gone.

300
00:19:05,960 --> 00:19:09,517
Gone but then I realized I didn't
have to live with the way she was.

301
00:19:09,600 --> 00:19:11,217
Murder is part of this game.

302
00:19:11,300 --> 00:19:15,077
If I couldn't have the Yuuki I loved
back, I'd settle for the memory of her.

303
00:19:15,160 --> 00:19:16,597
And who could blame me?

304
00:19:16,680 --> 00:19:19,417
That's why you did it.

305
00:19:19,500 --> 00:19:21,457
That's the reason you killed your wife.

306
00:19:21,540 --> 00:19:22,917
It's reason enough.

307
00:19:23,000 --> 00:19:26,057
And someday you'll understand too.

308
00:19:26,140 --> 00:19:29,317
Once you've found love, believe me.

309
00:19:29,400 --> 00:19:31,165
You'll do anything to keep it.

310
00:19:32,720 --> 00:19:34,197
You're wrong, Grimlock!

311
00:19:34,280 --> 00:19:36,237
You've got it all wrong!

312
00:19:36,320 --> 00:19:38,577
You didn't love Griselda.

313
00:19:38,660 --> 00:19:40,177
That's not what you felt.

314
00:19:40,260 --> 00:19:43,907
You stopped loving her when you
became selfish and possessive.

315
00:19:56,820 --> 00:19:59,237
Kirito, we appreciate your help.

316
00:19:59,320 --> 00:20:01,657
But I think this is our
problem to deal with now.

317
00:20:01,740 --> 00:20:02,570
Okay.

318
00:20:20,980 --> 00:20:21,810
Hey.

319
00:20:22,580 --> 00:20:25,237
Say it was you, and you married someone.

320
00:20:25,320 --> 00:20:29,980
And later on, you found out she had
a side tour you didn't know about.

321
00:20:30,520 --> 00:20:31,638
How would you feel?

322
00:20:34,100 --> 00:20:36,300
I guess that I was lucky.

323
00:20:38,240 --> 00:20:39,070
Because,

324
00:20:39,153 --> 00:20:40,817
I mean, if you marry someone,

325
00:20:40,900 --> 00:20:43,557
that means you already like whatever
you know about them, doesn't it?

326
00:20:43,640 --> 00:20:45,537
And if you discovered
something you didn't know

327
00:20:45,620 --> 00:20:47,617
about them before and fell
in love with that too,

328
00:20:47,700 --> 00:20:49,400
then that would be awesome.

329
00:20:51,100 --> 00:20:52,400
Right, good answer.

330
00:20:52,980 --> 00:20:54,980
Anyway, I'm hungry after all this.

331
00:20:55,320 --> 00:20:57,437
I didn't really get to finish my dinner.

332
00:20:57,520 --> 00:20:59,600
Oh, yeah, he didn't.

333
00:20:59,940 --> 00:21:02,058
We should get back to work tomorrow.

334
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:04,497
We've been off the front
lines for two days.

335
00:21:04,580 --> 00:21:09,168
Yeah, I was hoping to have this floor
totally cleared by the end of this week.

336
00:21:10,860 --> 00:21:11,690
Now what?

337
00:21:45,080 --> 00:21:46,237
Hey, Kirito.

338
00:21:46,320 --> 00:21:47,791
Do you want to friend me?

339
00:21:49,180 --> 00:21:50,820
It's kind of silly not to.

340
00:21:51,260 --> 00:21:52,201
It's convenient.

341
00:21:52,520 --> 00:21:54,577
We are in the same assault team after all.

342
00:21:54,660 --> 00:21:56,740
But I'm a solo player.

343
00:21:57,240 --> 00:21:59,737
Hey, I didn't say you had
to form a party with me.

344
00:21:59,820 --> 00:22:02,077
You should try to make some
friends while you're here.

345
00:22:02,160 --> 00:22:03,157
Yeah, I don't know.

346
00:22:03,240 --> 00:22:04,337
It's not that I don't want...

347
00:22:04,420 --> 00:22:05,250
Hey!

348
00:22:05,333 --> 00:22:06,397
Think about it while we eat.

349
00:22:06,480 --> 00:22:07,310
No pressure.

350
00:22:07,700 --> 00:22:10,197
Come on, let's go back and
find a good restaurant.

351
00:22:10,280 --> 00:22:11,460
Uh, okay.

352
00:22:24,660 --> 00:22:26,895
I'm not even going to be a little bit.

353
00:22:30,340 --> 00:22:40,177
I'll be strong again.

354
00:22:40,260 --> 00:22:42,497
I'll be

355
00:22:42,580 --> 00:22:44,277
strong

356
00:22:44,360 --> 00:22:51,360
again.

357
00:23:36,580 --> 00:23:38,660
The temperature of the heart.
